"During a multi-vendor network migration where we're transitioning from Cisco to Nokia 7750 SR routers, I need to ensure consistent BGP route selection behavior—particularly when dealing with routes that don't have the MED attribute populated. Since Nokia 7750 SR's implementation defaults to treating missing MEDs as infinite values, what's the recommended approach to maintain predictable path selection across our peering sessions while avoiding suboptimal traffic flows?"

