To ensure backward compatibility with legacy BGP peers using 2-byte ASNs while preventing 4-byte ASN negotiation on Nokia 7750 SR routers, apply the following configuration at the appropriate BGP hierarchy levels for the affected peers:

### For Group-Level Configuration:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "LEGACY_PEER_GROUP"
        disable-4byte-asn
    exit
exit
```

### For Specific Neighbor-Level Configuration:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            disable-4byte-asn
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key Details:
1. **Hierarchy Flexibility**: The `disable-4byte-asn` command can be applied globally under `config>router>bgp`, per peer group under `config>router>bgp>group`, or per neighbor under `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor`.
