To implement BGP route damping on your Nokia 7750 SR routers to suppress unstable prefixes while preserving stable path advertisement, follow these steps:

1. **Define a route policy with damping parameters** (adjust thresholds based on your network requirements):
```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement "BGP_DAMPING_POLICY"
    entry 10
        damping
            half-life 15         // Penalty half-life (minutes)
            reuse 750            // Reuse threshold (penalty must drop below this to re-advertise)
            suppress 3000         // Suppress threshold (penalty must exceed this to be suppressed)
            max-suppress 60       // Maximum suppression time (minutes)
        exit
    exit
commit
```

2. **Apply the damping policy globally to BGP**:
```cli
/configure router bgp
damping "BGP_DAMPING_POLICY"
```

### Key Threshold Recommendations:
- **Half-life**: 15 minutes (penalty decays by half every 15 min)  
- **Reuse**: 750 (re-advertise routes when penalty drops below this)  
- **Suppress**: 3000 (suppress routes when penalty exceeds this)  
- **Max-suppress**: 60 minutes (maximum suppression duration)  

These values balance rapid suppression of flapping routes (≥3 flaps within 15 minutes triggers suppression) while allowing stable routes to converge normally. Penalty decay ensures suppressed routes automatically re-emerge when stable.

### Verification Commands:
```cli
show router bgp routes damping [suppressed | damped]  // View affected routes
show router bgp routes <prefix> detail                // Check penalty metrics
```

Adjust thresholds based on observed flap frequency in your network. Lower `reuse`/`suppress` values increase sensitivity, while higher values reduce false positives.
