To implement BGP dampening with tuned parameters on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, configure a custom damping profile and apply it globally to BGP. Adjust the half-life to **10 minutes** and increase suppression thresholds to reduce impact on stable routes:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
    damping "FLAPSUPPRESS" 
        half-life 10
        max-suppress 40
        reuse 1500
        suppress 3000
    exit
/configure router bgp
    damping "FLAPSUPPRESS"
exit
```

**Key Parameters Explained:**  
- **`half-life 10`**: Penalties halve every 10 minutes (faster decay than default 15 min).  
- **`reuse 1500`**: Re-advertise routes when penalty drops below 1500 (less aggressive than default 750).  
- **`suppress 3000`**: Suppress routes only when penalty exceeds 3000 (higher than default 2000 to avoid over-suppression).  
- **`max-suppress 40`**: Maximum suppression time capped at 40 minutes (4x half-life).  

**Verification Command:**  
```cli
show router bgp damping-parameters
```

**Adjustment Guidance:**  
If stable routes still experience delays, incrementally increase `reuse` (e.g., `2000`) or decrease `suppress` (e.g., `2500`). For faster recovery, reduce `half-life` to `5` but monitor stability.
