## Proposed answer:
To prevent propagating learned BGP paths back to a specific customer VPN group on Nokia 7750 SR routers, configure a BGP group for the customer peers with a consistent Site of Origin (SoO) extended community. This ensures routes learned from one group member are tagged and blocked from readvertisement to other members.

```cli
configure service vprn <service-id>
    bgp
        group "CUSTOMER_GROUP"
            neighbor <peer-ip>
                site-of-origin <soo-value>
            exit
            neighbor <peer-ip>
                site-of-origin <soo-value>
            exit
            # Repeat for each neighbor in the group
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Replace placeholders**:  
- `<service-id>`: VPRN service ID for the customer VPN.  
- `<peer-ip>`: IP address of each customer BGP peer.  
- `<soo-value>`: Identical SoO extended community for all group members (e.g., `123:123`).  

**Effect**: Routes learned from any group member are tagged with the shared SoO. When advertising to other members, routes matching their configured SoO are automatically suppressed. Non-group peerings remain unaffected.
