To address the BGP route withdrawal propagation delay, configure the hold-time to 3 seconds with a minimum threshold of 3 seconds. Apply this at the group or neighbor level for targeted peers:

**Group-level configuration:**  
```  
/configure router bgp group "group-name"  
    hold-time 3 min 3  
```  

**Neighbor-level configuration:**  
```  
/configure router bgp group "group-name" neighbor ip-address  
    hold-time 3 min 3  
```  

**Key details:**  
- The `hold-time 3` sets the session to expire after 3 seconds without keepalives, triggering immediate withdrawal.  
- `min 3` ensures sessions are rejected if peers propose hold-times below 3 seconds, maintaining stability.  
- Replace `group-name` and `ip-address` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP.  

**Note:** This configuration accelerates failure detection but may cause session resets if keepalives are delayed. Test during maintenance windows and coordinate with peers to ensure compatibility with the 3-second hold-time.
